.TH V32LIBC 3v32 "October 19, 2026" "v32c++ 20261019-dev" "v32c++ Library"
.SH NAME
v32libc \- standard C library functions for C programs transpiled by v32c++
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.RB "(or " stdlib.h ", " ctype.h ", " errno.h ", " limits.h ", " memory.h ", " signal.h ,
.RB " " stddef.h ", " unistd.h ", " fcntl.h ", " sys/types.h ", " sys/stat.h ")"
.PP
.B #include <v32libc.c>      \fR/* once, in the program's one source file */
.PP
.B v32c++ \-I \fI<v32c++>\fB/libc program.c\fR      (no \fB\-I\fR once v32c++ is installed)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A C program transpiled by
.BR v32c++ (1)
from a
.I .c
file can use the part of the standard C library listed below, written
for the console and transpiled together with the program. Every one of
the standard-named headers in
.I libc/
includes the same declarations header,
.IR v32libc.h ,
so a program keeps its
.B #include
lines as they are. Because Vircon32 programs are one translation unit
with no linker, the code itself is brought in by including
.I v32libc.c
once.
.PP
.I v32libc.h
also includes the SDK's
.IR video.h ,
.IR input.h ,
.IR time.h ,
.I string.h
and
.IR misc.h .
Where an SDK function already behaves as C says, it is used as it is:
.BR strlen ,
.BR strcmp ,
.BR strncmp ,
.BR isdigit ,
.BR isalpha ,
.BR isupper ,
.BR islower ,
.BR isspace ,
.BR tolower ,
.BR toupper ,
.BR memset ,
.BR memcpy ,
.BR memcmp ,
.B rand
and
.BR srand .
Where it does not, the standard name is a macro for a conforming
.B v32_
function (see
.BR "STANDARD NAMES REDIRECTED" ).
.PP
.BR <string.h> ", " <time.h> ", " <math.h>
and the other SDK header names always reach the SDK's own headers, never
this library; the declarations below come with any of the
.I libc/
headers.
.SS Words and the null pointer
Everything is one 32-bit word:
.BR char ,
.BR short ,
.BR int ,
.B long
and every pointer, so
.B "sizeof(char) == sizeof(int) == 1"
and a string is an array of words. Code that writes \(lqthe 4 bytes of
an int\(rq
.RB ( "fwrite( &n, 1, 4, f )" )
touches three words too many and must say
.B sizeof n
instead.
.PP
The null pointer is 0, as in C; v32c++ rewrites null pointers and
pointer tests in C input to make it so. The SDK, however, uses \-1 for
\(lqno pointer\(rq: do not pass a C null pointer to an SDK function
directly.
.SH STANDARD NAMES REDIRECTED
.TP
.BR malloc ", " calloc ", " realloc ", " free
Return 0 on failure, accept
.B free(NULL)
and
.BR realloc(NULL,\ n) ,
over the SDK's allocator (see
.BR misc.h (3v32)).
.TP
.BR strcpy ", " strcat ", " strncpy ", " strncat
Return their destination, as C's do.
.B strncpy
writes exactly
.I n
words, padding with zeros, and leaves no terminator when the source is
.I n
characters or longer.
.TP
.B exit
See
.BR "PROGRAM FLOW" .
.SH STDIO
.TP
.BR printf ", " fprintf ", " sprintf ", " vsprintf
Formatted output. Conversions:
.BR %d ", " %i ", " %u ", " %x ", " %X ", " %o ", " %c ", " %s
and
.BR %% ,
with the
.B \-
and
.B 0
flags, a width and a precision (either may be
.BR * ),
and the
.B h
and
.B l
length modifiers, which change nothing since every integer is one word.
There are no floating-point conversions.
.TP
.BR putchar ", " puts ", " fputs ", " fputc ", " putc
Character and line output.
.TP
.BR getchar ", " fgets
Read from the on-screen keyboard (or the program's own key source; see
.BR v32term (3v32)),
echoing to the screen.
.B fgets
reads only from
.BR stdin ;
Backspace deletes, and Escape or Enter ends the line.
.TP
.B sscanf
.BR %d ", " %u ", " %x ", " %c ", " %s ,
with the
.B h
and
.B l
modifiers and a width.
.TP
.BR fflush ", " setbuf
Output is not buffered;
.B fflush
on a memory-card file writes it back.
.B setbuf
does nothing.
.TP
.BR fopen ", " fclose ", " fread ", " fwrite ", " fgetc ", " getc ,
.TQ
.BR fseek ", " ftell ", " rewind ", " feof ", " ferror ", " remove ", " rename
Files on the memory card; see
.BR v32file (3v32).
.TP
.B perror
Print a message and
.B strerror(errno)
to the screen.
.PP
.BR stdout " and " stderr
write to the 80\(mu24 text screen of
.BR v32term (3v32),
and
.B stdin
reads its keyboard.
.SH STRINGS AND CHARACTERS
.TP
.BR strchr ", " strrchr ", " strstr
Search a string.
.TP
.BR isprint ", " isalnum ", " ispunct ", " iscntrl ", " toascii
Character classes missing from the SDK (ASCII).
.TP
.BR atoi ", " abs
Conversion and absolute value.
.B abs
is a macro for the library's own
.BR v32_abs ,
so it never collides with the
.I math.h
of the SDK, included or not.
.SH ERRORS AND SIGNALS
.TP
.B errno
Set by the file functions:
.B ENOENT
(no such file),
.B ENOMEM
(out of memory),
.B EACCES
(the memory card holds another game's data),
.B ENODEV
(no memory card),
.B EMFILE
(too many open files),
.B ENOSPC
(the memory card is full).
.TP
.B strerror
A message for each of those.
.TP
.B signal
There are no signals on a console:
.B signal
remembers nothing and returns
.BR SIG_DFL .
The
.B SIG
constants exist so that programs compile.
.SH TIME
.TP
.B time
A number that changes every second: the console's date and time of day
combined. It is not the number of seconds since 1970, but it serves as
a random seed and as input to
.BR localtime .
Compiling with
.B \-DV32LIBC_FIXED_TIME=\fIn\fP
makes it always return
.I n
(for reproducible test runs).
.TP
.B localtime
The console's current date and time as a
.BR "struct tm" ,
whatever its argument.
.B tm_wday
is always 0.
.SH ENVIRONMENT AND PROGRAM FLOW
.TP
.B getenv
Always
.BR NULL ;
.B environ
is empty.
.TP
.B main( argc, argv )
v32c++ calls
.B main
with
.I argc
1 and
.I argv
.RB { \(dqprogram\(dq ", " NULL }.
A program that defines
.B "char **v32_main_args( int *argc, char **argv )"
has it called at the top of
.BR main ,
and can choose its own command line there (from a title screen, for
example).
.TP
.BR exit ", " abort
Show
.B v32_exit_prompt
(\(lq[Press START to play again]\(rq), wait for Start on gamepad 1,
clear the screen and restart the program from the beginning, with RAM
cleared and globals initialized again. If
.B v32_exit_hook
is set, it is called first with the exit status.
.SH LIMITS
.BR INT_MAX ,
.BR INT_MIN ,
.BR LONG_MAX ,
.BR LONG_MIN ,
.B SHRT_MAX
and
.B PATH_MAX
(256) are defined;
.B UINT_MAX
equals
.B INT_MAX
and
.B CHAR_BIT
is 32. The types
.BR size_t ,
.BR time_t ,
.BR off_t ,
.BR pid_t ,
.BR uid_t ,
.B gid_t
and
.B mode_t
are
.BR int .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <v32libc.c>

int main( int argc, char **argv )
{
    char name[ 32 ];

    printf( "What is your name? " );
    fgets( name, sizeof name, stdin );
    printf( "Hello, %s", name );
    printf( "%d arguments, first is %s\en", argc, argv[ 0 ] );
    printf( "[%5d] [%\-5d] [%05x]\en", 42, 42, 255 );
    exit( 0 );
}
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <installed include dir>/libc/
.IR v32libc.h ", " v32libc.c ", " v32file.c ", " v32term.h ", " v32term.c ,
.IR curses.h ", " v32curses.c ,
and the standard-named headers. The installed include directory is
.I /usr/local/Vircon32/v32tools/include/v32c++
by default; C input searches its
.I libc/
automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR v32file (3v32),
.BR v32term (3v32),
.BR v32curses (3v32),
.BR v32c++\-headers (3v32),
.BR misc.h (3v32),
.BR v32c++ (1)
.PP
.I docs/C_INPUT.md
in the v32c++ source distribution.
.SH AUTHOR
Matthew Haas
